 "about_text": "Make Room is a contemporary art gallery in Hollywood, Los Angeles, founded in 2018 by collector and curator Emilia Yin. It occupies interconnected exhibition spaces with an outdoor courtyard and garden. The program centers on artists exploring cultural identity, conceptual practice and global perspectives, often ahead of institutional recognition, with a stated commitment to female artists, artists of color and voices working outside established centers. Shaped by Yin's position between Los Angeles and Asia, the gallery has introduced emerging artists and reframed established ones, including Terence Koh, Sun Woo, Andrew Sendor, Guimi You, Yeni Mao, Tuan Vu, Xin Liu and Jacopo Pagin. Works by its artists have entered major public collections including LACMA, the Hammer Museum and the Institute of Contemporary Art Miami.",
